<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kosmoi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The kosmoi were the chief magistrates of the city-states of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a> compared the constitution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> with those of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and Crete, drawing an analogy between Carthaginian institutions and the Spartan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephor">ephors</a> and Cretan kosmoi. The comparison appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s profile in discussing Carthage's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixed-constitution">mixed constitution</a>.</p></div>
